			"date": "2025-08-04T13:24:34.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I've started using Eleventy Image for the first time today, for the photos on my new Eleventy site, for example on <a href=\"https://activites.nicolas-hoizey.com/activites/2025/07/28/dijon-tournus-jour-4/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">activites.nicolas-hoizey.com/a</span><span class=\"invisible\">ctivites/2025/07/28/dijon-tournus-jour-4/</span></a></p><p>And my own weird trick to reduce build times by 99&nbsp;% is to use `urlFormat` (only for production builds) so images are resized and optimized by Cloudinary… 😅</p><p>As this is my first time, I didn't find if there's a way to define settings per template, of even better a HTML container, instead of attribute overrides on each image. 🤔</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114970967369822106",
			"parentId": "114970714100169178",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/114970967369822106",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-08-04T14:28:59.408Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> the transform method does use attributes, yeah. If you’re wanting programmatic access to each image transformation, the transform method is likely not for you. (use the shortcode method instead?) I’d subscribe to something like <a href=\"https://github.com/11ty/eleventy-img/issues/248\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/11ty/eleventy-img/i</span><span class=\"invisible\">ssues/248</span></a> for future work there</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
